MagicNet fork patch: let sniffing hand the domain name to the outbound.

Why this has to live in the fork
--------------------------------
MagicNet's transparent inbounds (tun and ebpf, both tagged `tun-in`) only see
packets addressed to an IP address. sing-box sniffing records the TLS SNI or
HTTP Host in `metadata.Domain`, which route rules can match on, but
`ConnectionManager.NewConnection` always dials `metadata.Destination`. That is
the resolved IP, so a proxy node never learns which domain the app wanted and
cannot do its own domain based split routing.

sing-box used to expose `override_destination` on the sniff action for exactly
this. `RouteActionSniff` and `RuleActionSniff` still carry the field, the three
call sites in `route/route.go` still honour it, but 1.14 dropped it from the
JSON schema, so the field can never be set from a config file and the runtime
check is dead code.

This patch reintroduces the option and keeps UDP working:

* `option/rule_action.go` accepts `override_destination` again.
* `route/rule/rule_action.go` passes it through to the runtime action.
* `route/route.go` remembers the packet destination in
  `metadata.RouteOriginalDestination` before replacing it with the domain.
  Without that the NAT rewrite for packet (UDP/QUIC) connections has no origin
  address to restore and replies would come back from the node's own egress
  address.
* `route/conn.go` retries once with the remembered destination when a domain
  dial fails, so a node that cannot resolve a sniffed name degrades to the
  previous IP based behaviour instead of failing the connection.

MagicNet only ever emits the option on a TCP scoped sniff rule, and only when
the running core advertises the capability, so UDP keeps its current path.

Apply with `scripts/apply-sing-box-patches.sh`, then commit the result in the
fork and bump the `sing-box` gitlink. The module build refuses a dirty
submodule on purpose, so the patch must not stay uncommitted.
